      "id": 1,
      "text": "Gautier takes its name from Fernando Upton Gautier, who opened a sawmill on the Pascagoula River in 1867.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.gautier-ms.gov/198/Our-History-Folklore",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town grew around that sawmill, and its historic home, called “The Old Place,” still belongs to Gautier family descendants.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gautier%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Eric Clark Coastal Preserve, a 900‑acre protected area opened in 2023, offers hiking trails through Gautier’s wetlands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gautier%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Gautier is part of the Pascagoula Metropolitan Statistical Area, linking it to the larger Gulf Coast region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
